00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.690
And I'm wondering if maybe Democrats, I don't
want to say should give up on some issues,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.070
but may be a lost cause.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.980
I want us to talk about specifically gun control.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:50.469
Um, I'm wondering if the resources we use
and specifically getting assault weapons bans,

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:56.430
magazine capacity bands are, are, you know,
I see a lot of people in the community, especially

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.460
the gun community, they want to counteract
these laws and the second amendment sanctuary

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.159
cities, you know, I guess my question to you
is, is should we not focus more on women's

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:11.400
rights, gay rights, stuff like that and whether
or not any legislation we get in, I mean,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.700
what are the chances of it being able to be
held up, especially with the Washington DC

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.700
band being overturned?

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.880
No, I think that, so a couple things.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.889
Number one, we should be fighting for everything
all the time because they can't stop everything.

00:01:24.889 --> 00:01:28.439
First and foremost, that's, that's the, that's
just a reality that we have to understand.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:33.100
Number two, remember the Supreme court does
not hear every case.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.909
And so a lot of these things take a very,
very long time to really be good to get all

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:39.340
the way up to the Supreme court.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.789
If the Supreme court is even going to hear
it, particularly if we're able to remove Donald

00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:48.770
Trump in 2020, we'll have a, a, a democratic
house.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.490
Even with a Republican Senate, there are still
things that can be done.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.319
There are things that can be done at the state
level.

00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:59.539
Uh, universal background checks is one that,
um, uh, is less likely that the Supreme court

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:04.389
would even choose to get involved in because
there, there appears to be at least far less

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:07.139
constitutional argument there.

00:02:07.139 --> 00:02:10.670
And so I, I reject the idea that we shouldn't
be fighting these things.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:11.670
Sure.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.860
We have a conservative Supreme court and depending
on what happens in November of 2020, it may

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.420
become even more conservative, but the Supreme
court is not going to stop everything.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.250
It is not going to hear every case.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.519
And there is huge progress that can be made.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:30.090
Uh, and it's, it is sort of, I mean, listen,
it's hard enough to get stuff done at the

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:35.799
